WEBVTT

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:38.480
Let's spread our wings and flutter away,
and awaken from the dream of a thousand years.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.910
You're in a good mood, Ryuubi-dono.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:48.120
I got my sword back!

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:54.130
I know you're happy, but that's dangerous.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:59.890
Those clouds look nasty. Lightning
could strike at any second.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.220
You're scared of thunder? What a kid!

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.150
No, that's not it.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.030
Look!

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.020
That's what happens when
you get hit by lightning.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.200
Lightning often strikes metal objects,
so be careful, everyone!

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.560
<b>Episode 9
Gakushin, Riten, and
Ukin Protect a Village</b>

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.880
There's a village.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.240
Whew! Let's sleep there tonight!

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.020
Yeah. Any minute now, it could rain.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.560
I'd much prefer to sleep
somewhere with a roof.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.400
Stop!

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.360
Who are you?

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.910
Who are we?

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.320
We're just what we look like:
a group of travelers.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.290
Travelers?

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.790
I see weapons. You're not bandits, are you?

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:17.170
Ironic. The black-haired bandit hunter
herself mistaken for a bandit...

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.010
The black-haired bandit hunter?

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.580
Liar!

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.220
I heard the black-haired
bandit hunter was a real beauty!

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.950
It can't be you!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.490
Aisha, they're just children.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.100
I know.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.120
I know, but...

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.820
Call Gakushin-san and her gang!

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:39.000
Right!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.190
They seem pretty spooked by something.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.340
I'm sure there are bandits around here...

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:48.600
That doesn't mean it's OK to suspect us!

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:54.990
If only Aisha were as hot as rumored,
this wouldn't have happened.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.500
Sorry that I'm not good enough.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.060
Ukin-san!

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.630
Riten-san!

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.350
Maou-chan, it's gotta be them.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.560
OK!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.890
Take this, bandits!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.370
I'm so sorry.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.370
I'm sorry we jumped to conclusions.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:38.220
It's fine... As long as you know it was
a misunderstanding, we're happy.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.340
Raise your head, Gakushin-san.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:46.550
Maou and Sawa didn't mean any harm.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.380
Yeah. I only did it because you
were screaming about bandits!

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:54.640
But the gate guards ran up, and when
I asked what had happened,

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.480
they said bandits were attacking-

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:02.990
Um, you seem quite worried about bandits.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.850
Did something happen?

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:10.950
You see, we were on our way to Sousou-dono's
land, seeking a commission in her army.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.620
To Sousou-dono's?

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.540
Yes. We've heard that Sousou-dono
is a noble lord,

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:22.500
who will take in any with talent,
regardless of their original station in life.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:31.250
We stopped here for shelter. That night,
the bandits lurking in the mountains attacked.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:35.770
It seems every village male has been
drafted for war or forced labor,

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:39.010
leaving only children and the elderly.

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:45.610
Apparently, the bandits want to exploit that,
to make this village their new fortress.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.820
Stupid bandits!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.850
Since then, the bandits attack whenever
they think we're vulnerable.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:59.010
Each time, we chase them away, but there
are just too many for us to defeat.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.340
We spend our days strengthening
our defenses.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.880
I see.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.800
So that's what's going on.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.950
It's been three months since we came here.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.020
Bandits have attacked us ten times...

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:16.640
To be honest, we can't stay here forever.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.170
But we can't abandon the others, either...

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:21.270
Of course we can't!

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:25.030
Should they control this village,

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:30.240
they'll grow even stronger and start to attack
the other surrounding villages and towns.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:31.720
Aisha.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.280
I'll help you, too.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.830
I can't do much, but I can weave mats!

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:43.340
Then I'll take those mats and
roll up the bandits in them!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.670
But from what you've said,
the bandits have the numbers.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.060
We'd be at a disadvantage
in an open fight...

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.010
Shuri, any ideas?

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.850
This drawing is all we have.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.850
It's plenty.

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:02.940
This is the village, and this is the
bandits' mountain hideout.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.820
This is the bridge in front of the village...

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.100
Is this a lake up here?

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:15.440
Yes. Because a dragon god is said to dwell
there, it's called the Dragon God's lake.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.650
According to the villagers,

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.790
it used to be a fairly large lake.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:26.170
But the water level's dropped, and the river
in front of the village has thinned a lot.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.280
What is it, Shuri?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.590
Any ideas?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:38.560
Yes... If we could gain the
Dragon God's aid, we might be all right.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.870
The Dragon God's aid, huh?

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:06.840
Koumei-dono has proven a far more proficient strategist
than she appears, but what does she have in mind?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.200
Then you made this device?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:12.970
Yup.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.750
You bend a thin steel rod like this,

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:19.430
and it uses the power of
the spring to fire things.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.770
I see...

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.350
You're great at making things!

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:28.500
Yup! If I've got the parts, I
can make most anything.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.860
Then you like the three Chou sisters, too?

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:32.820
Yes!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.320
I saw them along my journey,
and I fell in love!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.100
Me, too!

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:41.000
Their dances and songs are
so cute, I love them!

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.880
Their outfits are great, too!

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.460
They are! They are!

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.150
What's wrong, Ryuubi-dono?

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:18.740
Can't you sleep?

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.370
I'm sorry.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:24.200
I was thinking of my blade, and
I just couldn't fall asleep.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.170
Your blade?

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.420
Yes.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.570
My mom always used to tell me

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:32.640
that I had many noble and
famous ancestors.

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:36.380
And, to serve the people, they
all took this sword in hand.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:41.850
So, since I was to inherit it, I
would need to do the same.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:46.700
But I never really understood
what it meant.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:51.320
I couldn't even take care of myself,
let alone serve the people...

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:52.780
You know?

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.280
Yeah...

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:02.820
But, on my journey, I've met people like
these villagers or those orphans,

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:06.000
and I've learned that there are
many people suffering in this world.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:11.700
I don't know what I can do,
but I've decided I must do something.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.100
I see...

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:17.850
Then up until now, we've been companions
on a journey to recover your sword,

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:21.650
but from now on, let's be companions trying
to make the world a better place.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:24.680
Okay!

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.570
I've spent the day studying the layout,

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:33.860
and I think we'll be able to enlist
the Dragon God's aid.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.820
Listen, everyone.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:43.370
First, we'll build a floodgate here, to dam in the water
flowing from the Dragon God's lake into the river.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:49.370
Even if there isn't much water,
if we dam it, the lake will fill eventually.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:52.320
And from what the elders
in the town were saying,

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:57.210
every year about this time,
there's a month-long rain.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:01.400
Which means we won't have to wait
too long until we're ready.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:07.990
Once the lake is full, we'll strike the bandits'
hideout at night with a small force.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:12.770
When they counterattack, we'll
draw them back to the bridge.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:18.240
Once we've crossed it, we'll drop the bridge
to lure them into the dry riverbed.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:21.420
Then we open the floodgates?

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:28.660
Yes. If it works, while we may not wipe them all out,
we'll neutralize a large number of them.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.420
A hard rain, huh?

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:33.710
We'll wash 'em all away!

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:35.180
Yep!

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:48.810
Well? Not bad, huh?

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:52.350
Yes! I don't know how you put something
so nice together in so few days!

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:56.350
Riten-san, you really are
a construction genius!

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:00.570
Aw, you don't mean it.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:05.030
Now we just wait for the river to fill.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:11.000
It would be nice to have the Dragon
God's blessings by now.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.210
Speaking of the Dragon God,
that stone over there...

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:18.900
I heard this from the villagers who
helped me with the floodgate.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:24.180
That's supposedly a dragon egg,
and if it breaks, a dragon will emerge.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:29.820
A dragon egg?

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.720
Lately, it's been raining every day.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:52.610
Yup... But thanks to this rain, the
lake's going to fill up faster.

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:53.920
We can't complain.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:58.010
But once the lake's full, we'll fight again.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:03.460
Actually, I really don't like fighting.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:08.920
I tell myself I need to work hard
to beat the bad guys...

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:11.970
But I'm so scared, I start shaking.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:15.720
On our journey, the three of us
have fought bandits and stuff,

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.720
but I always slow the others down.

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:20.760
The other two try so hard,
I feel I'm pathetic.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.870
That isn't true.

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:27.200
You're scared, but you're holding
it in and doing your best.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.710
So I think you're trying even
harder than the others.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:32.870
It's not pathetic at all.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:35.790
Ryuubi-san...

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:40.240
And I'm sure I've been more of a hindrance
on my journey than you have.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:43.300
If you don't believe me, you can
ask Kan'u-san and the others.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:47.180
I don't think that's something
to be proud of.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.970
Come to think of it, you're right.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.680
Welcome back!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.950
How was the lake?

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:56.850
Great!

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.940
It's filled.

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:02.150
We attack tonight.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:08.520
I'm going to have you attack
the bandits' hideout now.

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:10.000
Leave it to us.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.960
Our goal is to lure out the enemy,

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.620
so don't go in too far.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.600
Riten-san, you stay by the floodgates.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:22.630
Ryuubi-san is in the woods between
the lake and the village,

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:26.120
on standby, waiting to relay
my signal to Riten-san.

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:28.970
When the water comes, I'll sound the gong.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.260
When you hear it, get away from the river.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:33.430
Right.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:40.620
OK, then. Good luck, everyone!

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:51.560
Rin Rin, don't chase after them.

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:54.160
Our goal is to lure them out.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.470
Got it!

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.370
You sure?

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.640
Are you OK?

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.430
O-Of course!

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:27.160
Gakushin-dono!

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:28.370
Right!

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:29.300
Sawa!

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.580
Got it!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.050
Rin Rin! You, too!

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:36.550
Let me go!

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.790
I want to hit more people!

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:45.160
Boss, they're falling back!

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:49.290
I bet they thought they surprised us,
but our numbers are far too great.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:52.630
OK! Follow them, and let's hit the village!

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.890
Tonight's the last night we sleep outdoors!

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.860
Boss, look at that!

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.400
Fools.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:10.560
Don't worry, the river's not that deep!

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:12.210
Charge!

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.670
I'm first-

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:31.980
It's about time.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.510
That's the signal.

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:44.510
Go! Go! Go!

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.640
Aisha, is the flood here yet?

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.560
We won't last much longer.

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:53.320
I know!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:55.530
The signal again?

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.720
The flood hasn't hit yet?

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:03.520
Did something happen to Riten-san?

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:21.050
Riten-san, what happened?

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:22.730
Open the floodgate...

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.620
What is this?

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:31.580
When I opened the floodgate,
that stone fell into the ditch.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:34.630
The rain must have loosened the ground.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:40.430
I tried to move it, but no matter
what I do, it won't budge.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:42.200
Damn it!

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.380
If I'd known this would happen,

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:48.030
I'd have gotten rid of that rock
when I was making the floodgate!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:12.930
Idiot!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:16.110
That's not gonna be enough to shatter it!

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:23.020
Move!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.770
You fool!

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:33.970
You were about to get fried!

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.990
No! We need to run!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:56.210
You knew that would happen?

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:59.150
Good! It worked...

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:02.490
H-Hey, wait!

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:14.510
Sawa!

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:15.740
Okay!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:44.130
Sawa!

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:45.530
Hurry!

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:46.510
Right.

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:51.100
B-Boss!

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:06.230
Rin Rin, help me!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.410
Sawa...

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:36.700
The water dispersed overnight.

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:37.500
Yeah.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.090
We got most of the bandits, too.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.020
<i>And they all lived happily
ever after!</i>

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:44.190
I wish...

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:45.730
But Ryuubi-dono's...

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:46.510
Yeah.

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:53.020
Ryuubi-dono, why not head back
to the village for now?

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:56.060
The villagers said they'd help.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:59.620
You can look for your sword
after you get some rest.

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.140
It's OK.

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:05.130
When the lightning struck, the
blade was burned black.

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:07.950
Even had I found it, it wouldn't
have been useable.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:14.150
Ryuubi-dono, I'm sure you're saddened,
having lost the sword you finally regained.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:19.840
But your desire to change the world
for the better, to help the people,

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.420
did you lose that with your sword?

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.030
Riten told me of your deeds.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:30.920
Putting yourself in danger and trying to save
the village, even if it cost you your sword...

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:34.220
I'm sure your ancestors would applaud that.

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:42.250
You lost your sword, but I believe you inherited
something even more important.

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:43.900
Kan'u-san...

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.160
The first night, when we arrived,

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:52.210
I told you that we were companions on a journey
to make the world a better place.

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:56.330
So, if I can help you with anything, tell me.

00:21:57.320 --> 00:22:02.210
Umm... Then, can I ask you something?

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:03.550
Of course!

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:07.470
Kan'u-san, would you make
me your younger sister?

00:22:08.780 --> 00:22:12.110
Your words made me realize

00:22:12.110 --> 00:22:16.240
I will follow you the rest of my
life, to change the world!

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:17.850
So make me your younger sister!

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:19.980
No way!

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:22.840
Aisha's only sister is me!

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:28.860
Y-Yeah, Ryuubi-dono, I already have a bratty
little sister, so I don't need any more.

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:32.410
You won't?

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:36.910
But maybe you could be her older sister.

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:38.750
Really?

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:40.670
Rin Rin, what are you-

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:42.820
Very well.

00:22:42.820 --> 00:22:45.670
Then I'll be your older sister!

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:47.910
Wait a second...

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:49.640
And they all lived happily ever after!

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:54.260
<i>No!</i>

00:24:26.200 --> 00:24:27.310
Welcome!

00:24:27.310 --> 00:24:30.410
I'm your <i>Tencho</i> who never
turns down interviews, Riten.

00:24:30.410 --> 00:24:33.670
I'll take extra-spicy ramen,
with red-peppers.

00:24:33.670 --> 00:24:37.080
We're having a special. You can have rice or
a <i>preview.</i> Which do you want?

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:37.780
I'll take the rice.

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:40.000
No, I said rice or a <i>preview.</i>

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:40.770
And I said I wanted the rice-

00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:42.030
Order coming up!

00:24:42.030 --> 00:24:44.820
Extra-spicy ramen, with red peppers,
and a <i>preview </i>topping.

00:24:44.820 --> 00:24:45.710
OK!

00:24:45.710 --> 00:24:47.630
<i>Preview</i> coming up!

00:24:47.630 --> 00:24:50.320
Next time on <i>Shin Koihime
Musou,</i> Episode 10:

00:24:50.090 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Episode 10
Koumei Wishes for a Sister</b>

00:24:50.320 --> 00:24:52.680
Koumei Wishes for a Sister.

00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:55.010
But... I asked for the rice...

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Watch us again, OK?
And rewatch this episode!</b>
